SampleFreqSet waits until the display reaches line 159, so timer 0 starts in step with the
VBlank. In the WebAssembly build VCOUNT moves only inside VBlankIntrWait, so the wait never
ends and the game hangs in m4aSoundInit before its first frame. No timer drives the sound in
the build: the VBlank handler calls m4aSoundMain, whose SoundMain the glue forwards to the
port's mixer (rom/gen3/wasm/src/irv_wasm_sound.c), once per frame. Timer 0 has nothing to align,
so under IRV_WASM the wait goes.

diff --git a/src/m4a.c b/src/m4a.c
index 08f0531..a7f0fff 100644
--- a/src/m4a.c
+++ b/src/m4a.c
@@ -406,11 +406,13 @@ void SampleFreqSet(u32 freq)
 
     m4aSoundVSyncOn();
 
+#ifndef IRV_WASM
     while (*(vu8 *)REG_ADDR_VCOUNT == 159)
         ;
 
     while (*(vu8 *)REG_ADDR_VCOUNT != 159)
         ;
+#endif
 
     REG_TM0CNT_H = TIMER_ENABLE | TIMER_1CLK;
 }
